## Provenance

- The connector contract (URI dispatch, Atom shape, page→atom mapping) is a
  port of the Khan fork's `connectors/notion.py` + `connectors/base.py`
  (https://github.com/duketopceo/khan), itself MIT-licensed work by
  Luke Kimball / duketopceo.
- Khan's connector yielded `Atom` objects for an ingestion registry; this
  plugin keeps the same atom shape in `helpers/atoms.py` and adds the
  agent-facing half the issue asked for: a local stdio MCP server whose
  tools (search / get_page / get_page_content / query_database) surface
  inside stock a0 through `settings["mcp_servers"]`.
- Secrets stay in a0's vault (`usr/secrets.env`, `§§secret()`): the spawned
  server resolves the token inside its own process — `mcp_servers` carries
  none.

